# Paths excluded from secret scanning.
#
# NOTE: titus --ignore REPLACES its built-in defaults, so the usual build/vendor
# noise has to be listed here explicitly.
#
# Rationale: solver output is not hand-authored and is expected to contain
# exploit code, credentials from challenge services, and CTF flags. Scanning it
# produces hundreds of findings that are all working-as-intended, which buries
# real findings in the code and infra we actually control.
#
# Everything hand-authored stays in scope — including deploy/ and scripts/,
# where the two real secrets found during release prep actually lived.

# --- solver / competition output (expected to look "malicious") ---
challenges/
archive/
solvers/patterns/
findings.jsonl

# --- dependency + build noise ---
.venv/
.direnv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
result
.worktrees/
.playwright-browsers/
.playwright-cli/
.playwright-mcp/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- lockfiles: upstream hashes and URLs, no authored secrets ---
uv.lock
flake.lock

# --- scanner's own datastore ---
titus.ds/
